{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>His enemies</b> — Albesh said: the enemies of David. The opposite: he will clothe [them with] shame. [It is] the reverse of [the fact that] he will clothe [them with] salvation, the priests who pray on his behalf. And the word נזרו returns to the word [in the phrase] אצמיח קרן לדוד." "<b>His crown will sprout</b> — like יצא ונראה (went out and appeared), and similar to it: מציץ מן החרכים (peering through the lattice)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 132, :notes {0 "Resolved אלביש as a proper name (commentator) based on context; the passage is compressed and the argument structure is terse."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:39.255916627Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}